+
+## Driver scope and receipts
+
+`../terra-rust` has SQLite and feature-gated embedded TerraBase local-durable, single-client, closed-loop callers. Their receipts cannot close the above rows until equivalent guest execution, c4/open-loop where declared, full resource accounting, and Firecracker evidence are present. Each lane reports its own measurements without manufacturing a paired ratio. The SQLite 64-MiB page cache and TerraBase 128-MiB process admission budget cover different memory scopes; record both separately under the common 8-GiB guest envelope and compare measured whole-guest resources. A matched-cache physical comparison requires separately specified equal allowances and evidence. `terra-rust/README.md` specifies exact invocation and the adapter operation contract. Save completed raw JSON receipts and human-readable result tables in `bench/` with the matrix version, case ID, trial, and source identities.
+
+The P03/P04 diagnostic hypothesis is registered before an engine scan change: the current run reader may repeat directory/metadata access and point lookup for every output row or tombstoned key. Capture the current source-matched TerraBase and SQLite baseline plus guest scan-work counters first; report raw per-scan work and resources as well as latency. Use paired one-operation `--scan-diagnostics` runs for process CPU and I/O deltas, separate from unprofiled repeated throughput/latency trials; unavailable counters stay missing rather than becoming zero. Record immutable-run count, checkpoint sequence and mutable bytes before measurement; `--checkpoint-fixture=false` means only that the driver did not request a final checkpoint. P04 must verify the empty/sparse result and enforce a harness timeout so a large deleted history cannot hang qualification. An optimization is evaluated only after that evidence, and these rows remain open until repeated paired trials and the full gates above pass.
